  [
    id 59
    label "n9YsQeUp1qY"
    step 0
    date "2021-05-23T16:15:02Z"
    title "10 Dead Celebrities Who Are Actually ALIVE (Elvis Presley, Adolf Hitler, Tupac, Justin Bieber)"
    description "10 Dead Celebrities Who Are Actually ALIVE&#10;&#10;Subscribe for the best funny videos! inspired by AzzyLand, SkyDiverge, ItsOwen, Best Trends, Kwebbelkop, Gloom, Reaction Time &#38; Infinite - Top 5 Awesome&#10;&#10;#celebrity #celebrities #conspiracy&#10;&#10;Related Videos:&#10;&#10;Dead Celebrities Who Are Actually Alive:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8eraNZHM1to&#10;Top 10 Famous People Who Tragically Died While Performing:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=x2JzKy5c6PY&#10;Top 10 Dead People Rumored to be Alive:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2PwN_kPrZbM&#10;Top 10 Dead People Rumored To Still Be Alive:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zwRtdyWd7Qc&#10;Top 20 Hidden Celebrity Movie Cameos You Missed:&#10;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YojQ-Q0dJkg&#10;&#10;Top 10 Dead Celebrities Who Are Actually Alive&#10;When a celebrity dies, it&#8217;s headline news. One of the biggest bits of gossip, no matter how morbid it is, is celebrity death. Some people even go as far as to participate in Celebrity Death Pools, in which they bet on and predict which celebrities will die this year. People all want to know the details of celebrities&#8217; deaths, including who died, when and how. It&#8217;s no surprise that some enterprising individuals have created celebrity death rumors and hoaxes because of this. Here are the Top 10 Dead Celebrities Who Are Actually Alive. You&#8217;ll want to stick around til the end because the number one entry will surprise you! &#10;&#10;10. Paul McCartney: You may be thinking that no one in their right minds would believe that one of the members of the famous British band, the Beatles, was dead, But there actually is a conspiracy theory that states that Paul died in a car wreck in 1966 and was then replaced with a look-alike by British military intelligence agencies. The band has since released several weird nods to the conspiracy that appear to be breadcrumbs. George Harrison give &#8220;advice for those who die&#8221; in The Taxman, supposedly referring to Paul. Sgt. Pepper&#8217;s Lonely Hearts Club Band was an album in which they formed a totally different band with a new fictional member called Billy Shears, played by &#8220;Paul&#8221;. John Lennon&#8217;s A Day In The Life was featured on the album, containing the lyrics &#8220;He blew his mind out in a car&#8221;. If you play the song backwards, &#8220;Paul is dead. Miss him, miss him,&#8221; can be heard. And Lennon mumbled &#8220;I buried Paul&#8221; at the end of Strawberry Fields Forever. Another thing that believers of the conspiracy theory point to as proof is their album art. Yesterday and Today&#8217;s cover displayed the band amid random dismembered doll parts and bits of raw meat, which could represent the gruesome crash scene. If you place a mirror over the Sgt. Pepper album over the word Lonely Hearts on the drum, you can read &#8220;1ONE 1X HE DIE1 ONE1&#8221;. And then there&#8217;s the infamous Abbey Road cover in which the band members reenact a funeral procession. John represented the clergyman dressed in white, Ringo was dressed in black and represented the mourner, George wore jeans and represented the gravedigger and Paul walked out sync with the others, wearing no shoes because the dead don&#8217;t need them. Did Paul really die in 1966? Who is the impostor we&#8217;ve been following all this time? The world may never know! &#10;&#10;9. Avril Lavigne:  Avril Lavigne achieved fame at the age of 18, singing hits like &#8220;Sk8ter Boi&#8221; and &#8220;Complicated&#8221;. But she doesn&#8217;t seem like the same person as that sweet, punk girl. Some people think that&#8217;s because Avril committed suicide in 2003. There are various reasons for this sited, such as the pressure of fame, her parents&#8217; divorce and her grandfather&#8217;s death. So, then who is this person posing as Avril? That&#8217;s supposedly a look alike named Melissa Vandella. Fans of this theory point to differences in the singer&#8217;s facial expressions, clothing style and voice. They suggest that Avril preferred pants and Melissa prefers skirts and dresses. And they point to song lyrics, such as &#8220;The day you slipped away I found out it won&#8217;t be the same&#8221; in her song &#8220;Slipped Away&#8221;, and &#8220;Don&#8217;t leave me hanging in a city so dead. Held up so high by such a breakable thread&#8221; in &#8220;My Happy Ending&#8221; as clues that Melissa is leaving to Avril&#8217;s death. She was once photographed with the word Melissa written on her hand, as well. So, whether Avril is Avril or Melissa is still up for debate."
    channeltitle "Top 5 Awesome"
