  [
    id 136
    label "BjFllXhAP5Y"
    step 0
    date "2015-07-21T18:12:23Z"
    title "USA: MEMPHIS: ELVIS PRESLEY IMPERSONATORS MOURN HIS DEATH"
    description "(15 Aug 1997) Japanese/English&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Fans are flooding Memphis, Tennessee, by the tens of thousands to mourn Elvis Presley, the man who gave birth to rock'n'roll.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;These days, Presley is the most impersonated performer in the world, from Toledo to Tokyo.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;And as anticipation mounts ahead of the 20th anniversary of his death, impersonators are strutting their stuff in his hometown.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;The spotlight shines on a vision in gold filling up the stage.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;With a shimmy, and a swivel of his hips, a young Elvis Presley breaks into song - and hundreds of fans break into applause while the competition checks him out.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Saturday is the 20th anniversary of the death of the King of Rock'n'Roll.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;And Elvis impersonators from around the world are drawn to Memphis - like sequins to his legendary white jumpsuit.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;They say they're here to pay tribute to their hero, but they're also here to win.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;92 Elvis &#34;wannabes&#34; are competing in this contest for the grand prize of one-thousand U-S dollars.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;So they glue on the fake sideburns, struggle into the white jump suits and prepare to be Elvis.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;You don't even have to really look like Elvis to do Elvis. &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;You can be any age, sex or nationality. &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;All you need is a love for the King. &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Naoto Ogata came call the way from Tokyo, speaking little English but knowing all the words to &#34;Blue Suede Shoes&#34;.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;For him, it's the fulfillment of a lifelong dream.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;SOUNDBITE: (Japanese) &#13;&#10;&#34;My dream was to visit Memphis and sing a song... an Elvis tune.&#34;&#13;&#10;SUPERCAPTION: Naoto Ogata, Japanese Elvis Impersonator &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;But why the love for an entertainer who died when this impersonator was just a child?&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;SOUNDBITE: (Japanese) &#13;&#10;&#34;He's cool, the hair, the sideburns. He's cool.&#34;&#13;&#10;SUPERCAPTION: Naoto Ogata, Japanese, Elvis Impersonator &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;These men are not seeking fame and fortune - but a chance to step outside of their every day lives lures people from all walks of life to step into the shoes of the Elvis.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;What do their friends and families say....  &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;SOUNDBITE: (English) &#13;&#10;&#34;Elvis is dead.&#34;  &#13;&#10;SUPERCAPTION: Walt Sanders, American Impersonator &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Elvis may be dead, but the crowd seems more than willing to set aside their disbelief and relive happier days.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;SOUNDBITE: (English) &#13;&#10;&#34;Tonight they were pretty calm. But a lot of the times you'll get in a show and they'll literally rip your clothes off. They just want a little piece of you to take home, to remember you, or get it under their fingernails or something. They literally do. I had an outfit ripped right off my back one night.&#34;&#13;&#10;SUPERCAPTION: Danny Galbincea, Elvis Impersonator &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Galbincea says he knows the reason behind the Elvis mania.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;SOUNDBITE: (English) &#13;&#10;&#34;I think its that they don't want to let go off Elvis and anything in a jumpsuit will suffice. That's about as close as I can put it. Once you put the jumpsuit on the transformation becomes complete and you can &#13;&#10;pick up just about any girl you wanted.&#34;&#13;&#10;SUPERCAPTION: Danny Galbincea, Elvis Impersonator &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;In a few hours the music will stop, but for now Elvis Presley is still in the building.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Find out more about AP Archive: http://www.aparchive.com/HowWeWork &#13;&#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/AP_Archive &#13;&#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/APArchives &#8203;&#8203;&#13;&#10;Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/APNews/&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;You can license this story through AP Archive: http://www.aparchive.com/metadata/youtube/1986761e8d03c7d237a05a46fe2a5771"
    channeltitle "AP Archive"
    channelid "UCHTK-2W11Vh1V4uwofOfR4w"
