    id 162
    label "W2l8QUSrT0A"
    step 0
    date "2021-05-30T23:00:06Z"
    title "Young Judy Tylers Death Nearly Broke Elvis Presley"
    description "Judy Tyler was born as Judith Mae Hess on October 9th, 1932.  From a young age, Judy was destined for a lifetime of fame. &#10;&#10;&#9644;Contents of this video&#9644;&#10;00:00 - Introduction&#10;00:50 - Early Career&#10;01:43 - Her Shot at Fame&#10;02:58 - Her Move to Hollywood&#10;04:00 - Jailhouse Rock&#10;06:09 - Tragedy Strikes&#10;&#10;Like this content? Subscribe here: https://www.youtube.com/factsverse?sub_confirmation=1  &#10;&#10;Or, watch more videos here: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLkXAntdjbcSKgHx6EQVOwNKVz1cR2hKVw&#10;&#10;Judy Tyler spent the vast majority of her youth living and working in New York City. Just spent a lot of time working on Broadway and on television. Judy landed a role on a child TV show that slingshot her to fame. Judy was cast as a beautiful Indian woman on the show Howdy Doody and appealed to little girls everywhere. &#10;&#10;Judy Tyler is one of the most well-remembered actresses of her generation. From modeling to singing to even acting on Broadway, it was no doubt that Judy Tyler was a star. Judy worked her way up the ladder of fame for years before she finally had true success. Judy was cast for a role in an up-and-coming movie with Elvis Presley! Excited to start her career in film, Judy traveled to Hollywood with her new husband and began filming. Judy Tyler got her big break when she was cast as Elvis &#10;&#10;Presley&#8217;s love interest in the famous film. Elvis Presley and Judy Tyler met on set in 1957. The two actors hit it off right away and got to work on their upcoming film. Elvis and Judy became close friends during their time together on set. &#10;&#10;Unfortunately, just after filming had ended, Judy was tragically killed in an automobile accident! Though the accident shook the world, it hurt Elvis the most. Jailhouse Rock proved to be a huge hit in Hollywood, but sadly Judy would not be alive to read the raving reviews. It is no doubt that Judy would have been an even bigger star if she had lived. &#10;&#10;Over the years, Elvis had acquired a reputation as a ladies man who frequently became romantically involved with his co-stars. Since her passing, many questions have been raised about the true nature of the relationship between Judy Tyler and Elvis Presley. Watch this whole video to find out about Judy&#8217;s tragic accident and Elvis&#8217;s reaction!&#10;&#10;Young Judy Tyler's Death Nearly Broke Elvis Presley"
    channeltitle "Facts Verse"
    channelid "UCXZpQgX1897wYDLtvzmgyIA"
