    date "2022-06-25T10:00:25Z"
    title "The Truth About Elvis Presleys Relationship With Colonel Tom Parker"
    description "Elvis Presley shot to stardom as a rock 'n roll legend, a legacy that still continues almost 50 years after the King's death. But behind the music, behind the movie roles, and behind Elvis' odd proclivity for staying in the United States for his tours, was one man: Colonel Tom Parker. It's a name that sounds like it comes straight out of a carnival &#8230; and that's not too far off from the truth. Parker may have been a ruthless businessman who negotiated the deals that led to Elvis' unprecedented fame, but there was a lot more going on behind the scenes than people realized. Here's the real truth about Elvis Presley's relationship with Colonel Tom Parker.&#10;&#10;#ElvisPresley #RockAndRoll #TheKing&#10;&#10;Shady past | 0:00&#10;Elvis' manager | 1:18&#10;Meddled in Elvis' marriage | 2:36&#10;Influenced Elvis' movie career | 3:51&#10;Controlled Elvis' touring schedule | 5:00&#10;Bad experiences in the military | 6:04&#10;Complications after Elvis' death | 6:56&#10;Priscilla liked the Colonel | 8:07&#10;Parker saw dollar signs only | 9:08&#10;&#10;Read full article: https://www.grunge.com/897444/the-truth-about-elvis-presleys-relationship-with-his-manager-colonel-tom-parker/"
    channeltitle "Grunge"
