  [
    id 279
    label "u_Rnzq0wPFc"
    step 0
    date "2012-08-12T01:30:35Z"
    title "ELVIS PRESLEY Way Down 35 th Anniversary of the Kings death!"
    description "In August of 1977 'Way Down' by Elvis Presley was released in Australia. The song was recorded in late 1976 and released in America in June of the next year. It only reached a lowly peak of #31, before his death on August 16. After this incredible loss to the world of pop culture, the song climbed back and later reached #18.&#10;&#10;In Britain the track went to the Top of the Pops, and here in Australia - the song entered the Top 100 six days after his death and would travel all the way to #6, spending some 4 months in the Top 40.  His previous hit 'Moody Blue', also resurfaced - charting all over again. &#10;&#10;I don't recall too many pop culture deaths like that of Elvis Presley. Michael Jackson, John Lennon in the same class of shock and grief. Elvis was bigger than an icon - he was a phenomenon. His incredible charisma, perfectly chiselled face, distinctive vocal style and smouldering image made him a hero for generations - he still has a strong fan base - all these years later. The King is dead - long live the king!"
    channeltitle "daveinprogress3"
