    step 0
    date "2022-06-28T21:00:17Z"
    title "Elvis died of chronic constipation  #shorts #elvispresley #toilet #health"
    description "&#128293; ACHIEVE FAT LOSS FOR THE FINAL TIME &#9989;&#10;&#10;&#127942; with award-winning 1:1 tailored fitness, nutrition and mindset coaching here: https://www.bodysmartfitness.com/apply-now/?bsf=YTS_COPY&#10;&#10;Connect with us &#128071;&#10;&#129331; Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/bodysmartfitness&#10;&#128170; Team Body Smart: https://www.instagram.com/teambodysmart &#10;&#127925; TikTok https://www.tiktok.com/@bodysmartfitness&#10;&#127909; Main YouTube: https://www.youtube.com/c/BodySmartFitness&#10;&#10;&#127851; Lose 30lbs eating chocolate every day! Watch our nutrition masterclass: https://www.bodysmartfitness.com/masterclass/?bsf=VSL_YTS_COPY&#10;&#10;&#128231; If you downloaded our masterclass and it didn't show up in your inbox, contact hello[at]bodysmartfitnessl[dot]com &#10;&#10;&#10134; &#10134; &#10134;&#10;&#128561; Get ready to be All Shook Up!&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;Did you know chronic constipation contributed to Elvis&#8217;s death? Let us know in the comments &#128071;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#128148; The King succumbed to heart failure, which was in part caused by chronic constipation (a common side effect of opiates). &#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#128701; Constipation is common at all ages and caused by factors such as: &#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#10062; Not eating enough fibre&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#10062; Not drinking enough fluids&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#10062; Long periods of inactivity&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#10062; Stress, anxiety, and depression&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#10062; Certain types of medication&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#10062; Pregnancy&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#10062; Ignoring the urge to poo&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#128581;&#8205;&#9792;&#65039; For most people, constipation is nothing to worry about. &#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#128218; However, for people who suffer from chronic constipation, studies have shown it could be linked to cardiovascular disease (doi:10.1111/jch.13489, doi:10.1016/j.athersclerosis.2015.10.001, doi: 10.1111/jch.13489) &#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#128073; &#34;Strain at stool causes blood pressure rise, which can trigger cardiovascular events such as congestive heart failure, arrhythmia, acute coronary disease, and aortic dissection.&#8221; (doi: 10.1111/jch.13489)&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#128076; The good news is there are simple changes you can make to keep things Shake, Rattle, and Roll(ing). &#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#9989; Get at least 10-15g of fibre per 1,000 calories&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#9989; Drink plenty of water&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#9989; Move your body on a daily basis&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#9989; Reduce stress and anxiety where possible&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#128169; Last, but not least, if your body is telling you It&#8217;s Now or Never, listen to it and go have a poo. &#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#8201;&#8201;&#10;&#128680; Don&#8217;t let yourself fall victim to the Jailhouse Block."
