  [
    id 348
    label "ZBKbK2vQB5U"
    step 0
    date "2015-07-21T18:10:47Z"
    title "HONG KONG: ELVIS PRESLEY FANS MARK 20TH ANNIVERSARY OF HIS DEATH"
    description "(17 Aug 1997) English/Nat&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Elvis Presley fans gathered around the world to commemorate the 20th anniversary of the death of the King of Rock 'n' Roll on Saturday.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;In Hong Kong, the Elvis Fan Club held their own ceremony filled with souvenirs as well as performances by the territory's Elvis impersonators.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;It was exactly 20 years ago on Saturday when Elvis Presley, the King of Rock 'n' Roll. died.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;And his fans around the world have been marking the anniversary.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Here in Hong Kong, hundreds of Elvis fans turned up to enjoy an evening filled with singing and dancing to the tunes of the late King.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Each year, the Elvis Fan Club here organizes events to commemorate his death on August 16th as well as his birth on July 8th.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;This year, the highlight of the event were the Elvis impersonators.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;One of the most popular figures in Hong Kong is the territory's own &#34;Melvis Kwok.&#34;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;The Indonesian-born impersonator has built a career out of singing the King's songs.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;His acoustic renditions of Elvis' ballads always get a warm applause.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;He's been an Elvis impersonator for the last 5 years, and says the King brings him happiness and has helped him through hard times.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Also known as the &#34;Elvis of Hong Kong&#34; is Johnny Ma, the winner of several &#34;Elvis Impersonator&#34; titles.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;His made his 70s Elvis outfit himself.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Two Elvis devotees try to explain his attraction to Asian fans.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;SOUNDBITE: (English)&#13;&#10;&#34;A lot of Asians think that he's a good friend to them, in fact to myself I think he is my all-time friend because I have been an Elvis fan for nearly 20 years and, in fact, Elvis is my companion from growing up.&#34;&#13;&#10;SUPER CAPTION:  Vivian Tsang, President of Hong Kong's Elvis Fan Club&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;SOUNDBITE: (English)&#13;&#10;&#34;I think he's still in my heart.  I can make him (come) alive in Hong Kong, I think.&#34;&#13;&#10;SUPER CAPTION:  Melvis Kwok, Elvis impersonator&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Forty-five-year-old Ma has been impersonating Elvis for more than 22 years.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Fans say Ma's singing and dancing almost rivals that of the original King of Rock 'n' Roll Elvis Presley himself.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Find out more about AP Archive: http://www.aparchive.com/HowWeWork &#13;&#10;Twitter: https://twitter.com/AP_Archive &#13;&#10;Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/APArchives &#8203;&#8203;&#13;&#10;Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/APNews/&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;You can license this story through AP Archive: http://www.aparchive.com/metadata/youtube/6dc96850530b164e0adbd1f0ef54975c"
    channeltitle "AP Archive"
    channelid "UCHTK-2W11Vh1V4uwofOfR4w"
