    step 0
    date "2012-08-16T09:27:15Z"
    title "Elvis Presley Palm Springs Home: A Narrated Tour By Current Owner (Part 1)"
    description "A narrated tour of the Elvis Presley Palm Springs Estate at 845 W Chino Canyon, Palm Springs, California, by my good buddy Reno Fonana, who is the current co-owner of the former King of Rock and Roll's winter retreat from the Memphis winter. &#10;&#10;This is the only home Elvis owned other than Graceland at his death and spent about 2.5 months a year at this home.&#10;&#10;INTERESTING FACTS ABOUT THIS PROPERTY:&#10;&#10;Elvis spent his last birthday here;&#10;&#10;Elvis last visited this property a mere 26 days prior to his death;&#10;&#10;Elvis bought this property in 1970 with Priscilla after leasing another home nearby for a year.  &#10;&#10;The property was fairly looted upon the knowledge that Elvis had died in Memphis on August 16, 1977 and many possessions/artifacts were lost. &#10;&#10;When in Palm Springs, be sure to stop by and say hi. Paid tours are offered on a daily basis to the Elvis faithful. People even today still flock to the gates of what the New York Times once called, &#34;Graceland West&#34;."
