    title "Unchained Melody - Elvis Presley - 33 1/3 rpm"
    description "On June 21, 1977, just six weeks before his death, Elvis Presley performed &#34;Unchained Melody&#34; for what would be his last television appearance, &#34;Elvis In Concert.&#34; However, the recording that was ultimately released as a single and included on the Moody Blue album (the last released while he was alive) was from an earlier appearance at Ann Arbor, Michigan, featuring him on piano, as was invariably the case when Presley sang the song in concert."
