  [
    id 440
    label "mdk7q08FCJ0"
    step 0
    date "2022-07-09T11:52:46Z"
    title "The Ending Of  #elvispresley #austinbutler #elvismovie"
    description "Even when he was still alive, Elvis Presley, the King of Rock and Roll, was the stuff of Hollywood legend. A 19-year-old Memphis, Tennessee, truck driver takes the globe by storm with an explosive combination of Country music, Gospel, and Rhythm &#38; Blues. After dominating the charts, he goes on to dominate Hollywood, starring in over 30 films in just over a decade. And just when it appears that he has been washed up and forgotten, he returns to prominence with a television comeback spectacular in 1968.&#10;&#10;Many films about Presley's life, from John Carpenter's 1979 television movie starring Kurt Russell to the 2005 CBS miniseries, conveniently end at this point of triumph, eluding or outright ignoring the last decade of his life, when artistic stagnation and debilitating substance abuse issues turned The King into a clown. &#34;Elvis,&#34; the long-awaited biography from imaginative filmmaker Baz Luhrmann, arrives in 2022.&#10;&#10;For starters, no previous film about Elvis Presley has possessed Luhrmann's colorful, maximalist approach, a chaotic swirl of colour and sound aiming to convey the sensory assault Elvis' youthful followers must have had upon hearing his music for the first time. But, more significantly, Luhrmann and his screenwriters Sam Bromell and Craig Pearce don't gloss over the superstar's tragic last years, which he spent in a gilded Las Vegas cage at the hands of his manipulative manager, Colonel Tom Parker.&#10;&#10;As anybody who remembers the Old Elvis vs. Young Elvis postage stamp issue will attest, it's a period that many Elvis enthusiasts would want to forget. However, for Luhrmann, the era is not a postscript or an uncomfortable fact, but rather crucial to the film's singular point of view. Consider the conclusion of &#34;Elvis.&#34;"
    channeltitle "Share FYI"
    channelid "UCI3LqIS3yA97pF2dG1M5qaA"
    favcount 0
    viewcount 25370
    likecount 403
    commentcount 91
    duration "PT12M42S"
