he's being very evasive. Why? If her dad really dead , the answer to all these weird questions would be short and simple: &#34;No&#34; or &#34;No, and I don't want to talk about this&#34;. But every time , both Lisa and Priscilla have a hard time answering, because they avoid confirming that Elvis is dead ( because they know it's a hoax) and at the same time they cover him, they protect him and so they give ambiguous, evasive answers .&#10;&#10;Source LINKS:&#10;1. 1995 - Priscilla on Barbara Walters, at min. 14:10 - https://youtu.be/lMcX9jRHciU&#10;2. Montage from 2013 - https://www.facebook.com/197418280315197/photos/a.197864033603955/598629263527428/?type=3&#38;theater&#10;a) 2003 - Lisa on Larry King, at min. 04:32 - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=12ZtqWHhpfU&#10;b) 2005 - Priscilla on Oprah, at min. 00:23 - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N9kfUBG_NOY&#10;3. Montage from 2011 - https://www.facebook.com/197418280315197/photos/a.197864033603955/201522579904767/?type=3&#38;theater&#10;4. 2007 - Priscilla on Larry King&#10;- at min. 06:38 - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-zNhEyqOntA&#10;- at min. 02:10 - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=la66ik1LWvs&#10;5. 2018 - Lisa at min. 01:20 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e5TUWHogQIM"
